    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0845" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg757"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. McCormick.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-15"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 138.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s telegram of
                    July 27 last, and its No. 134 of July 29 last, relative to the United States
                    military <pb facs="0846" n="758" xml:id="pg758"/> stores on the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ardova</hi>, I inclose copy of a telegram from the
                    United States consular agency at Alexandria, Egypt, reporting that the captain
                    of the vessel had stated that the letter in his charge, addressed to the United
                    States quartermaster-general at Manila, had been taken from him along with the
                    ship’s papers.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d743-a1.xml" xpointer="d743-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
